# {{ package_name }}

Generated TypeScript SDK package.

Operations accept `(params, requestOptions?)`. Pass path, query, header, cookie,
and body inputs as named properties of the exported `OperationParams` type.
Transport settings such as headers, query overrides, and cancellation remain in
`requestOptions`. Request bodies use the `body` property, subject to collision
renaming in the generated interface.

Required inputs are required properties. When every input is optional, params
defaults to `{}`. Omit an optional property to leave it unspecified; explicit
`false`, `0`, and `""` are preserved. JSON null retains its normal meaning.

This calling convention replaces positional operation inputs from SDKs generated
by Arvalez 1. Input types are in `src/params.ts` and exported from the package index.
Raw and tag-grouped methods use the same input objects.


## Automatic pagination

When configured, collection operations expose lazy paginator and collect helpers.
They use the service pagination convention and per-operation overrides, including
starting page/offset, default/maximum page size, and the termination rule. All
filters and headers are retained. Collection fails if any page fails; use lazy
paging for incremental processing and early stopping.

Use `operationPaginator(...)` with `for await`. Each page is a typed item array. Await `operationCollect(...)` to collect everything. Both retain request options and abort signals.
